From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:02:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Shores: ground and rock where the wider view showed a forest
 over the sea and a forest on a rock (SDK_PORT_3DS)

East of Veilstone the forest's filler (matrix 563) has its first 8 rows of
trees standing over the sea, 3 tiles in from its west side: in the wider
view they floated. North of Solaceon the mountain's filler (586) is a rock
plain a tile above Route 210's forest with no side: the forest's first
column stood on the rock.

A shore is drawn along a line of points (in tiles): a strip of ground out
from the edge and a slope of rock down from it (or the rock first and the
ground at its foot), round or square corners where the line turns, the
textures by name from the area's set or from a loaded map's material
(Port_AreaTexture, Port_LoadedTexture). East of Veilstone: a grass strip
under those trees and along the forest's north side, square corners, its
edge all round Veilstone's own coast's (seaside3, the wavy dirt edge, lit
as the ground); all of it above 19, where Veilstone's model has a second
sea over that notch (and its north edge, drawn on north, takes it over the
sea's filler). North of Solaceon: the rock in two tiers, as Route 210's
cliff beside it, the upper to 40, a tile of grass at its foot; the plain's
last column of squares left out (sPortMapCuts) and drawn again as a strip
of its top behind the edge, only while the shore can be drawn
(Port_ShoreCutReady).
---
